        "original_id": "196a2d09-1170-5d07-93d6-8e5345a065d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Idrissa Ouédraogo, Jerry Paris\n- Films: Yaaba\n- Places: Banfora, Upper Volta, Burkina Faso, Africa\n- Roles: film director, actor\n- Topics: African settings, rural and city conflict, tradition and modernity\n\nFacts:\n- Jerry Paris was born on July 25, 1925, and he was an American actor and director.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was born on 21 January 1954 in Banfora, Upper Volta.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was a film director from Burkina Faso whose films were set within Africa.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo often explored conflicts between rural and city life and between tradition and modernity.\n- Yaaba is a 1989 Burkinabé drama film written, produced, and directed by Idrissa Ouédraogo.\n- Jerry Paris died on March 31, 1986.\n- Jerry Paris was best known for playing Jerry Helper, the dentist and next-door neighbor of Rob and Laura Petrie, on The Dick Van Dyke Show.",
